// ═══ LongAdder USAGE ═══
LongAdder counter = new LongAdder();
counter.increment();          // thread increments its own cell!
counter.add(100);             // add to own cell
counter.decrement();          // decrement own cell
long total = counter.sum();   // base + all cells (NOT atomic snapshot!)
counter.sumThenReset();       // sum + reset all to 0 (atomic per cell, not global)
counter.reset();              // reset all to 0

// ═══ HOW IT WORKS INTERNALLY ═══
// Low contention (1-2 threads):
//   CAS on 'base' variable → succeeds → fast! Like AtomicLong.
//
// High contention (16+ threads):
//   CAS on base FAILS (another thread beat us)
//   → Thread gets a Cell in the cells[] array (hash-based slot)
//   → CAS on own Cell → succeeds! (minimal contention!)
//   → Cell is @Contended → own cache line → no false sharing!
//
// sum(): return base + cells[0].value + cells[1].value + ...
//   NOT synchronized! Reads may miss in-flight increments.
//   Acceptable for: counters, metrics, statistics.
//   NOT acceptable for: balance (need exact real-time value).

// ═══ WHEN TO USE WHICH ═══
// AtomicLong: exact value needed in real-time (account balance)
//   get() returns the EXACT current value.
//   incrementAndGet() returns EXACT new value.
//   Under high contention: CAS retries → slower.
//
// LongAdder: high-write, read-occasionally (request counter, metrics)
//   sum() may be slightly stale during concurrent writes.
//   increment() is 5-10x faster under contention!
//   No get() that returns exact value — only sum().

// ═══ LongAccumulator — generalized LongAdder ═══
LongAccumulator maxPrice = new LongAccumulator(Math::max, 0);
maxPrice.accumulate(2450);
maxPrice.accumulate(2500);
maxPrice.accumulate(2480);
maxPrice.get();  // 2500 (maximum!)
// Same striping as LongAdder but with custom accumulator function!
